WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.402
-Our first guest tonight
as an Emmy-nominated actress,

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.871
writer, and director
you know from her

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.672
critically claimed
HBO series "Girls," as well as

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.109
her films "Tiny Furniture"
and "Sharp Stick."

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.478
Her newest movie,
"Catherine Called Birdy,"

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.546
is in select theaters
September 23rd

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.248
and on Prime Video October 7th.
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:18.184
-I've ridden all this way,

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.820
actually incurred several so-as
injuries during the process

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.323
because Hercules is broader
than you might imagine.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:25.792
So if you could just tell me --

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.326
-No, no, sir.
We know Lady Catherine.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.961
And you really
shouldn't have bothered.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:31.397
-We're just a bit confused
why you would travel this way

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.667
for such a --
-She's a creature.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:39.505
A vile creature. All teeth
and hair and vomit and snot!

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.542
-Some say she has a third ear.
-She does.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.510
-Have you seen this third ear?
-I've seen it.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.080
-Where?
-Back of her neck.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.815
-Is it functional?
-Spare.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:51.083
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.985
our friend Lena Dunham,
everybody!

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.787
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.787 --> 00:01:02.662 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:10.569 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:13.906
Lena, it has been way too long.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:18.010
-I am so happy to be back
with you, with Wally.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.113
-Yeah, it's nice of you.
Well, you know Wally well.

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:23.282
-Wally kind of became
a close friend of mine.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.017
And I feel like
we're still close.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.419
The pandemic couldn't stop it.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.554
-It couldn't break you apart.
-Nope.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.223
When I saw him today,
it was just, like,

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.724
love at first sight
all over again.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.026
-Wow. That's wonderful.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:36.462
He will definitely let us
all know that all week long.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:37.831
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.465
This is --
You were one of our guests

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:40.833
the very first week of the show,

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.635
which is why it's always
so lovely to have you back.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.737
-I love it,
I feel like an old-timer.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.005
And I'm just delighted.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.441
I love seeing the evolution
of your casualwear.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.309
-Thank you very much, yeah.

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.444
For a lot of people, this means
things are going worse,

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:54.947
but I actually feel
a little bit better.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.882
-I think it means you're
comfortable in your skin...

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.417
-Thank you.
-...and ready to roll.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:01.019
-You had some very big news
since I last saw you.

00:02:01.019 --> 00:02:04.657
You got married. I met
your lovely husband backstage.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:07.693
-Thank you.
Yep, he's here with me today.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.130
I feel very lucky.
He has an English accent.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.797
I can't believe
that happened to me.

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.867
-But it's -- it is fake, right?
It's a fake English accent?

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.602
-It's 100% fake.
-It's very good.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.571
-And I don't care.
-I can kind of hear

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.306
that there's something
a little off about it.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.809
-Yeah, he's basically Dirty
Johning me and I'm fine with it.

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:25.745
-You --
Also, this is actually

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.915
the most shocking to me,
is that you moved to London.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.951
Because I do consider you
a New Yorker --

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.585
like, one of the consummate
New Yorkers.

00:02:33.585 --> 00:02:34.920
-I -- I feel that way.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.556
And I have to say, while
I still do spend time here

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:40.426
and while I do have,
you know, a "home" here,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.062
I'm taking my London life
pretty seriously.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.997
-That's great. Do you feel like
they're accepting of you?

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:46.532
Do they like your vibe?

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:47.967
-No.
-Okay.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.635
[ Light laughter ]
-But I like their vibe,

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.237
and that's what matters.
-Oh, that's all that matters.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.339
-That's what matters.
-How long did it take to --

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.642
Was it immediately
that you caught their vibe

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.209
and said, "This is for me"?

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.612
-I have always been
a bit of an Anglophile.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.347
-Yeah.
I'm a little bit of that, too.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.815
-Are you that, too?
Like, when I was 8,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.184
I started calling my dad "Papa."
-Okay.

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.952
-For reasons that had --

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:10.756
you know, were absolutely not
a product of my household.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:13.359
And so it was a product
of reading "A Little Princess."

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:16.595
Shout-out to
Frances Hodgson Burnett.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:17.930
-Maybe -- You know what?

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.767
Maybe the first time she's been
shouted out on the show.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.268
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:25.138
-That's the job I want
and that I came here to do.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:29.175
So, yeah, I just always
had a sort of love

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:34.647
of all things sort of, you know,
Jane Austen, Bronte.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:39.051
You know, cobblestone streets,
carbohydrates.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:43.122
Everything that England
has to offer.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.424
And it turns out, love.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.958
-I'm so happy that you found

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.461
all those things
across the pond.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.998
That means -- You know.
-Oh, I know.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:54.100
-I also want to ask
about your dog.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.302
I want to ask because --
You know, so, I have a dog.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.104
She's a beautiful,
graceful creature.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.639
You know Frisbee, right?
-I know. I worship Frisbee.

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.674
-I get a lot of stick
on the show

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:05.945
because Andy Sandberg tells me
that she looks like a rat

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.614
and is very --
Yeah, very unattractive.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.083
And I would imagine --
Don't take this the wrong way.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.819
I imagine you might get that
sometimes about your dog.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.489
-Whatever do you mean, Seth?
-Okay.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.057
Your dog's name is --
-Ingrid.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.492
-Ingrid.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.727
Okay, and, again, please don't
take this the wrong way.

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:23.696
And I'm sure the audience
will respond in a way

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.598
that makes it clear
that I'm crazy for saying

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.166
that anyone
might ever be critical

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.968
of the way your dog looks.
-I know.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:34.173
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.608
Yeah.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.610
-Now, this, by the way,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.345
might be
who is Dirty Johning you.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.013
Because this is clearly --

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.483
This is clearly a child
in a dog suit.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.850
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.719
-I love that you say that,

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.353
because especially
during the pandemic,

00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:50.256
we were spending a lot
of time alone together.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.658
I would look at her, and be like
"Just speak already.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:55.595
Spit it out!
Say what you have to say."

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.363
I mean, I've had
some insane reactions to her.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.799
I was carrying her one day,
and an older woman asked me

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:02.802
where I got that "little goat."

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.771
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:08.907
My husband has taken to saying

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:11.176
that she's
a frog/seal combination.

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:14.580
Because he just can't
explain it to anyone anymore.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.284
-I will say, once you hear that,
it's hard not to see that.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.785
-I know. I know.

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:24.790
-You're like -- Yep.
A frog and a seal had a baby.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.393
-What's hard for me is that
people feel comfortable

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:31.898
on the street exclaiming about
how unattractive she is.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:35.635
And I'm like, "Would you ever
speak to a child this way?"

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.136
I mean, we were walking past

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.805
a group of teenagers,
English teenagers.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.572
And wait for my incredible
English accent.

00:05:40.572 --> 00:05:44.076
One was like -- [British accent]
"Oh, she's disgustin'."

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:47.113
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.516
And I was like,
"How dare you."

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.352
We had a party, and there
was a child at the party.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.887
It was my birthday party.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.790
I mean, she is the greatest gift
I've ever had.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.793
And my friend's kid
was sitting there being like,

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.262
"Mummy, she touched me!"

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.797
[ Laughter ]
And I just -- I don't get it.

00:06:05.797 --> 00:06:08.100
I feel when I look at her

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.870
that God
or whoever is controlling this

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.772
has taken all the qualities

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.440
I would find most appealing
in a creature

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.309
and just stuffed them all
together.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:19.078
I think she's so beautiful,
it makes me almost sick.

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:22.047
And when I first adopted her
and she was really tiny,

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:23.749
I used to carry her around
the West village.

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:26.018
It was winter.
In a baby snuggly.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.286
And so it was the best.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.754
I would be waiting
in line for coffee,

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.890
and someone would be like,
"Oh, my God."

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.626
And then look in the snuggly,
and it was like, boom, bitch.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.027
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.462
[ Applause ]

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:38.731
Like...

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.666
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:42.768
-And where did you come up
with the name Ingrid?

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:44.937
-Ingrid is named after --

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.439
you're going to be shocked
by this -- my friend Ingrid.

00:06:47.439 --> 00:06:51.978
And Ingrid Abrash is a lawyer
and a writer and a thinker

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:54.247
and a serious
animal-rescue enthusiast.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:55.982
-Okay, so she responded well

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.682
when she heard
she was being honored?

00:06:57.682 --> 00:06:59.018
-She told me to do it.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:01.153
She was like, "This is
the dog you should get

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:03.088
and I think
you should name her Ingrid."

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:04.923
-Alright.
Well, then that is a --

00:07:04.923 --> 00:07:07.727
That says a lot about the
character of your friend Ingrid.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:10.096
-That's exactly right. And she
thinks she's gorgeous, too.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.464
-Alright.
Well, there you go.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.132
I have a lot to ask about,
especially the movie.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.967
We'll be right back...
-Delighted to be back with you.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.702
-...with more from Lena Dunham.

